# Test: the suite's native le binary answers the RFC extraction envelope, the
# accept-only: the registered native fixture enforces this scenario's behavioral contract
# conformance check, audit re-seal, and requirement ledger over owned RFC inputs.
# Required actions retain their read/write markers without pinning registry size
# or descriptions. One authored summary and tagged unit own the expected counts;
# independent real-corpus verification still judges the whole production corpus.
#
# Page/JSON parity, cannot-run refusal, and the seeded untagged MUST discriminate
# the check's answers. No-op and shifted re-seals retain their byte-preservation
# and parity checks; index-update compares pages, all named artifacts, and JSON
# across independent copies. No writer changes the baseline inputs.
# Go's ordinary build cache is shared, never a cached action result.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-le-is-a-ze-binary AC-1, AC-7, AC-8 and AC-11 through the
# actual compiled developer-facing artifact and every supported rendering.

option=timeout:value=900s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture ui/le-rfc-answers
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
